(6066883, 891491, 97270, '<td valign="top">I understand what you tried to do here. It may have helped a bit more if it was close to night time, and you had the aperture closed to the farthest (f/16 or something) and you forced the ISO to a low value (100 or something) and then you had set the exposure time to a slightly longer one, so the effect of a longer exposure would be more evident.<br/> <br/>Original idea though, I give you a lot of credit for that!</td>', 'I understand what you tried to do here. It may have helped a bit more if it was close to night time, and you had the aperture closed to the farthest (f/16 or something) and you forced the ISO to a low value (100 or something) and then you had set the exposure time to a slightly longer one, so the effect of a longer exposure would be more evident. Original idea though, I give you a lot of credit for that!', '2010-06-23 01:36:44.000000', NULL, 0),
