(6067117, 891239, 112218, '<td valign="top">Hi there<br/>Beautiful pic.<br/>You have inspired me to get out and use my NDs - know what to do but procrastination....!!!!<br/>Thanks for the push!!!!</td>', 'Hi thereBeautiful pic.You have inspired me to get out and use my NDs - know what to do but procrastination....!!!!Thanks for the push!!!!', '2010-06-23 03:07:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067125, 891239, 63503, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!<br/>Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing.</td>', 'This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing.', '2010-06-23 03:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067128, 891417, 114969, '<td valign="top">Great work Brent, very nice finish :-) The background really makes the photo I think, nice choice of location, and great execution! Go Jawbones!</td>', 'Great work Brent, very nice finish :-) The background really makes the photo I think, nice choice of location, and great execution! Go Jawbones!', '2010-06-23 03:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067138, 890547, 29079, '<td valign="top">Congratulations...such a peaceful image...love the misty flow of the water around the front stones</td>', 'Congratulations...such a peaceful image...love the misty flow of the water around the front stones', '2010-06-23 03:17:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067156, 891239, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!<br/>Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Andres, that''s correct, I just double-checked my EXIF. why would you think it is strange? without the filter the exposure would be 1000x smaller, i.e. 1/1250s, quite normal for a bright daylight.</td>', 'Originally posted by senor_kasper: This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing.  Andres, that''s correct, I just double-checked my EXIF. why would you think it is strange? without the filter the exposure would be 1000x smaller, i.e. 1/1250s, quite normal for a bright daylight.', '2010-06-23 03:26:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067157, 891527, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is really great. I have rarely seen such a clear display of red and blue shifts in stars. It really enhances the 3D ''tunnel effect'' on your star trail circle.<br/> <br/>I don''t think that the city lights worked against you at all in this pic.</td>', 'This is really great. I have rarely seen such a clear display of red and blue shifts in stars. It really enhances the 3D ''tunnel effect'' on your star trail circle. I don''t think that the city lights worked against you at all in this pic.', '2010-06-23 03:26:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067165, 891532, 28710, '<td valign="top">Great job! Did you notice that the clouds almost take on the shape of a face looking down towards the bottom left? <br/> <br/>Great concept too. I wonder if the person in the center might have become even more surreal if you dodged the heck out of the bottom of the pants so it looks like it is totally made of light...</td>', 'Great job! Did you notice that the clouds almost take on the shape of a face looking down towards the bottom left?  Great concept too. I wonder if the person in the center might have become even more surreal if you dodged the heck out of the bottom of the pants so it looks like it is totally made of light...', '2010-06-23 03:30:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067173, 890547, 105957, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju með borðann Skarpi:-) Klárt mál að þessi vika er vika IMAGIO...5 myndir á forsíðunni:-D</td>', 'Til hamingju með borðann Skarpi:-) Klárt mál að þessi vika er vika IMAGIO...5 myndir á forsíðunni:-D', '2010-06-23 03:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067182, 891810, 28710, '<td valign="top">The exact perfect time. The happenstance of the darker horse behind is fortuitous and you couldn''t have asked for better lighting in the tail.</td>', 'The exact perfect time. The happenstance of the darker horse behind is fortuitous and you couldn''t have asked for better lighting in the tail.', '2010-06-23 03:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067184, 890547, 30214, '<td valign="top">congratulation Skarpi on your red ribbon! (we had similar ideas for this challenge, but rather different realizations :))</td>', 'congratulation Skarpi on your red ribbon! (we had similar ideas for this challenge, but rather different realizations :))', '2010-06-23 03:39:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067186, 891440, 28710, '<td valign="top">Wow. this is really strong!<br/> <br/>I really like the processing. I bet it would be really cool in a low sat as well. Maybe even a duotone... there''s a really nice balance between the smoothness of the water and the punch of the static areas. Might be cool if you worked with gentle colors to highlight the difference between the two sides of this image.<br/> <br/>A great idea - definitely working towards the ''impact''.</td>', 'Wow. this is really strong! I really like the processing. I bet it would be really cool in a low sat as well. Maybe even a duotone... there''s a really nice balance between the smoothness of the water and the punch of the static areas. Might be cool if you worked with gentle colors to highlight the difference between the two sides of this image. A great idea - definitely working towards the ''impact''.', '2010-06-23 03:41:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067191, 891521, 118194, '<td valign="top">wow, the last place. i''m not really surprised ;-)</td>', 'wow, the last place. i''m not really surprised ;-)', '2010-06-23 03:47:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067194, 890551, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is a standout image because it is very different, especially with colors, yet some of the choices you made are really interesting. <br/> <br/>I like the black flecks on the ''ground''. To me, they give a nice bit of grittyness that could be complemented very well with some large, soft monochromatic grain for a bit more ''retro'' feel.<br/> <br/>The unusual background is interesting too since it suggests the coloring of a night horizon. This is complemented by the cloud of smoke. This therefore suggests water for the bottom half and you end up with the suggestion of a landscape. <br/> <br/>Note the match box cover which has a classic feel, but contrasts with the overall color scheme of the pic.<br/> <br/>Very thought provoking and well done.<br/> <br/>PS. Classical guitarist?</td>', 'This is a standout image because it is very different, especially with colors, yet some of the choices you made are really interesting.  I like the black flecks on the ''ground''. To me, they give a nice bit of grittyness that could be complemented very well with some large, soft monochromatic grain for a bit more ''retro'' feel. The unusual background is interesting too since it suggests the coloring of a night horizon. This is complemented by the cloud of smoke. This therefore suggests water for the bottom half and you end up with the suggestion of a landscape.  Note the match box cover which has a classic feel, but contrasts with the overall color scheme of the pic. Very thought provoking and well done. PS. Classical guitarist?', '2010-06-23 03:50:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067201, 891236, 28710, '<td valign="top">Interesting. It seems like you have deliberately pushed the water way overboard for the dramatic feel (see challenge descript).<br/> <br/>I think it''s a bit much on the yellows and greens though. Bring it back 10% or so overall and 15-20% on the yellows and greens and I think it would still have that ''pushed hard'' look, but without toying with the edges of unpleasantness.</td>', 'Interesting. It seems like you have deliberately pushed the water way overboard for the dramatic feel (see challenge descript). I think it''s a bit much on the yellows and greens though. Bring it back 10% or so overall and 15-20% on the yellows and greens and I think it would still have that ''pushed hard'' look, but without toying with the edges of unpleasantness.', '2010-06-23 03:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067212, 891684, 43594, '<td valign="top">Love this one, glad you made it in top 10!</td>', 'Love this one, glad you made it in top 10!', '2010-06-23 04:15:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067218, 891398, 43594, '<td valign="top">This one is so beautiful, I like everything in it!</td>', 'This one is so beautiful, I like everything in it!', '2010-06-23 04:18:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067224, 891239, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations. Beautiful image.</td>', 'Congratulations. Beautiful image.', '2010-06-23 04:24:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067245, 891239, 63503, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by senor_kasper:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!<br/>Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Andres, that''s correct, I just double-checked my EXIF. why would you think it is strange? without the filter the exposure would be 1000x smaller, i.e. 1/1250s, quite normal for a bright daylight. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess 5.6 is really not all that small, I was probably intuitively thrown off by the apparent softness of the light which leads you to think of a cloudy day. You are correct regarding the math. Thank you for answering my question. <br/> <br/>Once again, GREAT IMAGE !!</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Originally posted by senor_kasper: This is a fantastic image, Lev. Congratulations !!Just one thing, are you sure it was a 10 stop ND? I would think 0.8 seconds with a 10 stop at f5.6/ISO 200 would have resulted in a nearly black image no matter how bright the sun was. Could you check it out please, it is intriguing.  Andres, that''s correct, I just double-checked my EXIF. why would you think it is strange? without the filter the exposure would be 1000x smaller, i.e. 1/1250s, quite normal for a bright daylight.   I guess 5.6 is really not all that small, I was probably intuitively thrown off by the apparent softness of the light which leads you to think of a cloudy day. You are correct regarding the math. Thank you for answering my question.  Once again, GREAT IMAGE !!', '2010-06-23 04:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067247, 891699, 52549, '<td valign="top">William, you ARE nuts ;-D  but, my God, you do incredible work. Love the story, love your work. Congrats on the blue and the great score.</td>', 'William, you ARE nuts ;-D  but, my God, you do incredible work. Love the story, love your work. Congrats on the blue and the great score.', '2010-06-23 04:57:28.000000', NULL, 0),
