(6067282, 891239, 105457, '<td valign="top">I was sooo glad that this got recognized in the DPC community, it''s so wonderfully done, great atmosphere, great scenario, and the water motion is just perfect.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on an awesome image!<br/></td>', 'I was sooo glad that this got recognized in the DPC community, it''s so wonderfully done, great atmosphere, great scenario, and the water motion is just perfect. Congratulations on an awesome image!', '2010-06-23 06:17:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067293, 891699, 118154, '<td valign="top">Super smashin'' well done to you ,love it !</td>', 'Super smashin'' well done to you ,love it !', '2010-06-23 06:42:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067304, 891239, 99263, '<td valign="top">Lovely image indeed. One question. It strikes me that you seem to have taken this shot from quite a high angle looking down on the girl and also from quite close to the girl. You used a 12-24mm lens. Were you standing on a lifesavers tower? (unlikely as lifesavers towers are not right on the edge of the water) Or maybe you are a giant and the girl is a dwarf :) But seriously, I would like to know.</td>', 'Lovely image indeed. One question. It strikes me that you seem to have taken this shot from quite a high angle looking down on the girl and also from quite close to the girl. You used a 12-24mm lens. Were you standing on a lifesavers tower? (unlikely as lifesavers towers are not right on the edge of the water) Or maybe you are a giant and the girl is a dwarf :) But seriously, I would like to know.', '2010-06-23 07:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067313, 890547, 90866, '<td valign="top">One great shot and I love the title.</td>', 'One great shot and I love the title.', '2010-06-23 07:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067322, 891780, 117474, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised you got such a symmetric pattern with a laser and string! It seemed too symmetric. I was thinking you had some machine moving the laser around.<br/>It was a great idea, and I thought it came out well. Did you have many tries at it?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-23 06:42:48.</i></td>', 'I''m surprised you got such a symmetric pattern with a laser and string! It seemed too symmetric. I was thinking you had some machine moving the laser around.It was a great idea, and I thought it came out well. Did you have many tries at it?', '2010-06-23 07:42:18.000000', '2010-06-23 07:42:48.000000', 0),
(6067339, 891690, 117717, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  Honestly, I was a bit surprised when I saw my mark in the 4''s... I really like the shot.  I wish I had the subject positioned a bit further from the wall.  I think that would have made her more distinguishable.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  Honestly, I was a bit surprised when I saw my mark in the 4''s... I really like the shot.  I wish I had the subject positioned a bit further from the wall.  I think that would have made her more distinguishable.', '2010-06-23 08:18:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6067343, 890547, 75241, '<td valign="top">Tl hamingju með þetta<br/>Einhvern veginn grunaði mig að þið Örvar Atli mynduð ná langt í þessari keppni.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-23 07:30:28.</i></td>', 'Tl hamingju með þettaEinhvern veginn grunaði mig að þið Örvar Atli mynduð ná langt í þessari keppni.', '2010-06-23 08:28:47.000000', '2010-06-23 08:30:28.000000', 0),
(6067346, 891379, 77305, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EBJones:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the vibrancy of your image, but I think that a longer exposure (to be more specific, more movement being evident in the grass and clouds) would have helped this fit the challenge better. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ya, that was the first thing I noticed when taking my first look at this shot on my computer. First shot taken with the Lee "Big Stopper" Next time!</td>', 'Originally posted by EBJones: I like the vibrancy of your image, but I think that a longer exposure (to be more specific, more movement being evident in the grass and clouds) would have helped this fit the challenge better.   Ya, that was the first thing I noticed when taking my first look at this shot on my computer. First shot taken with the Lee "Big Stopper" Next time!', '2010-06-23 08:35:54.000000', NULL, 0),
